ection. Actually collection 0 is weird. Let me check — maybe there's a conftest somewhere up the tree. The venv has pytest plugins. But default testpaths... Actually pytest collected 0 because there might be a `pyproject.toml` or `pytest.ini` upstream with testpaths restriction.\n\nLet me just rename tests.py to test_*.py which is the standard default collection, and also the table issue: tests use a fresh tmp_path db but `init_db` is called. The error \"no such table\" means init_db didn't run for the test db? Wait the fixture calls `db_mod.init_db(db_path)`. That should create the table. But the get_db uses the env var BOOKS_DB_PATH which we set via monkeypatch. So why no table?\n\nWait — actually the fixture creates db with init_db(db_path), but app uses db_mod.get_db() which reads DEFAULT_DB_PATH at import time (module-level). DEFAULT_DB_PATH = os.environ.get(...) was evaluated at import time! So monkeypatching env later doesn't change it. I need to make get_db read env each call, or pass db_path.\n\nLet me fix: make DEFAULT_DB_PATH computed lazily, or use app config. Better: store db path in app config.\n\nLet me refactor to use app.config[\"DB_PATH\"].\n\nAlso the collection issue: rename tests.py to test_books.py. Actually pytest default collects test_*.py and *_test.py. tests.py won't be collected by default unless configured. That's why 0 collected. Rename to test_books.py.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_eea2a8c06001z0fWy037LGI67p","sessionID":"ses_115d6a71bffepOnCGVBFSw3IFa","messageID":"msg_eea2a404b0010Vlc6jFvzco67V"}}
